## Language

Standard Scheme procedures are preloaded. The interpreter targets R7RS-small but is not fully compliant; describe exposes available procedures.
Imports are ignored. Inspect unfamiliar procedures and extensions instead of inventing them.
`length` takes a list; use `string-length` for strings. `string` constructs a string from characters, not arbitrary values.
Chatwoot objects use `hash`, `get`, `keys`, `hash-values`, `hash-set`, `hash-merge`, and `has-key?`.
map/filter take function FIRST and list SECOND; fold takes function, initial, list.
fold calls its function with ACCUMULATOR FIRST, ITEM SECOND: (fold (lambda (acc item) (append acc (list item))) '() items).
take takes LIST FIRST, COUNT SECOND: (take items 3). cons supports dotted pairs; Chatwoot tool arguments require proper lists/objects.
sort-by takes list, FIELD-NAME STRING, and "asc" or "desc", never a lambda or boolean direction.
Records contain a ref hash. fetch, related, and act take refs, not full records. IDs are database IDs.
Data and lambda bindings persist between execute calls and chat turns. Live control state such as continuations cannot be saved across turns.
Only #f is false; use `(null? values)` for empty lists.
Database null is distinct from #f and the empty list. Use (nil? value), never truthiness, to check nullable fields.
Parsing errors occur before evaluation; fix the syntax without changing selection or intent.
